    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0104" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710. Consultation (3)A/121: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chairman of the
                        Emergency Advisory Committee for Political Defense</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Guam</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-09-10">September 10, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of Your Excellency’s telegram of
                    September 2<anchor n="25" xml:id="d69-f1"/> informing me of the resolution
                    adopted by the Committee to investigate the activities of the Falange.</p>
                <p>My Government will endeavor to collect information of the character outlined in
                    the resolution for transmission at an early date to the Committee.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
